# Copy to .env and adjust. Never commit .env.
#
# This file must contain placeholder values only. Real credentials, tokens, and
# any PHI are prohibited in the repository (aidlc-e2e-rules.md §18, §19).
#
# The sibling NextGen Clinical suite ships real values in its own .env.example
# so it runs out of the box. We deliberately do not: "it is only a test key" is
# the reasoning that ends with credentials in every repository.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser (UI) scenarios — no credentials needed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Target environment: dev2 (default) | dev.
# The Clinical WebApp is deployed once per environment:
#   dev  -> https://clinical.dev.rethinkbhtech.com
#   dev2 -> https://clinical.dev2.rethinkbhtech.com
# dev2 became the default on 2026-08-25, matching the sibling suite's mandatory
# daily environment. An unrecognised value throws rather than falling back.
ENV=dev2

# Overrides ENV entirely when set. Use for a one-off target.
# If both are set they must agree, or the run throws — a run must never report
# an environment it did not actually target.
# BASE_URL=https://clinical.dev2.rethinkbhtech.com

# The UI needs no credentials. The dev environments authenticate through the
# /temp-dev-login route, which signs in without a username or password and
# redirects to /clients. Verified 2026-08-24; recorded in
# aidlc-docs/automation/REQ-CLIENT-001/framework-reuse-plan.md.
#
# The route name suggests it is temporary. If it is withdrawn, credentials
# belong here as environment variables and nowhere else, and
# src/fixtures/auth.fixture.ts is the only file that should need to change.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Clinical API — credentials required, and none are supplied here
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Only needed for `npm run api:readiness`. No test calls the API today: the
# tenant-scoped surface returns 503 (Accounts service), so setup and cleanup
# cannot be built against it. See aidlc-docs/automation/api-layer-plan.md.
#
# Ask the team for these, or take them from the sibling suite's configuration.
# API hosts are internal and may need the VPN.

# APP_KEY=
# SECURITY_KEY=
# AUTH_USERNAME=
# AUTH_PASSWORD=
# ACCOUNT_ID=
# DIVISION=bh

# Demographics "Client" user id, for the /clients/{clientId}/... routes.
# Optional — the readiness probe checks one more route when it is set.
# CLIENT_ID=

# Overrides the per-environment API host.
# API_BASE_URL=
